At some other place, at some other time, someone else wrote:

>Since Dragons are essentially the most dangerous animal in the game, and in
>fact the _only_ thing that is really capable of killing a really strong
>character who is resistant to poison, it seems like it is too easy to get rid
>of them for good.
>
 How about a couple of modifications.
 1.  Reading a scroll of genocide and specifying D results in random death
     of one type (color) of dragon.  Subsequent scrolls will then have a
     small chance of regenociding a color which is already gone.

 2.  I also have died by blasts of disintegration several times.  There is
     one particular bones level on our system which has a zoo with several
     disintegration dragons on it and many other dragons including at least
     one sleeping gas (maybe this is actually a dragon fart?? ;-) ) dragon
     I can usually wipe out 1 or two dragons on this level before death.
     We need a potion of disintegration resistance which wears off after
     a certain number of moves.  It should give some cryptic message when
     quaffed such as: You tremble and feel you have just escaped death!

 3.  Eating a dead dragon of any kind should give you intrinsic resistance
     to the effects of that particular type of dragon from then on.  Of
     course Gremlins still could chuckle and remove this ability.

 Just a few thoughts from a sick mind (too many potions of sickness I guess)

